# Project Rules

## Language

- **Code stays English.** All code, identifiers, file names, comments, commit
  messages, and assistant responses MUST be in English.
- **Site content is multilingual.** User-facing content may be localized into
  the supported locales: English (`en`, canonical source), Danish (`da`),
  German (`de`), and Swedish (`sv`). English is the source of truth; the other
  locales are translated from it.
- URL slugs are English by default; localized slugs are allowed only via the
  slug-pair mechanism in `src/data/lang.ts`.
- Product and brand names (the RoomAlyzer lines and product names) are NOT
  translated — they stay identical across all locales, with **three approved
  sensor exceptions** in German (`de`): "Water detector" → **"Wasserdetektor"**;
  "Outdoor" → **"Außen Sensor"**; "Range Extender and Bracket" →
  **"Range Extender und Bracket"**. Per-locale overrides live in
  `src/data/de-term-locks.json` and `src/data/deTermLocks.ts` /
  `src/data/sensorCategories.ts` (`localizedSensorName`); do not add others
  without explicit approval.
- **Module names** on `/de/`: five German overrides via `localizedModuleName()`
  (Raumklima, Erhaltung, Reinigung/Nutzung, Drucktasten, Schließfächer/Türen);
  **Space management** and **Water detection** stay English. See
  `src/data/de-term-locks.json`.
- When adding new content, write the English version first, then provide the
  translations (or rely on the English fallback) for the other locales.

### English copy style (`en`)

English user-facing copy uses **British English** and **sentence case**:

| Rule | Do | Don't |
|------|----|-------|
| **Spelling** | `optimise`, `licence` (noun), `centre`, `defence`, `utilisation`, `organised`, `anonymised` | American `-ize`, `-or` where `-ise`/`-our` is standard |
| **Capitalisation** | Capitalise only the first word and proper nouns/acronyms | Title Case on multi-word headings |
| **Product names** | Keep RoomAlyzer lines and catalogue names unchanged | Translate or re-case product names |
| **Plan tiers** | Single-word tier names stay as-is: `Building`, `Portfolio`, `Enterprise` | — |
| **URL slugs** | English slugs unchanged (`trust-center`, etc.) | Rename routes for spelling |

### Localization grammar (`da`, `de`, `sv`)

Non-English locales follow locale-specific grammar in addition to the product-name
rules below. Use `localizedSensorName()`, `localizedModuleName()`, and
`formatProductLabel()` for display names.

| Locale | Rule | Do | Don't |
|--------|------|----|-------|
| **German (`de`)** | Module names | Approved German names via `localizedModuleName()` (`Raumklima`, `Erhaltung`, …); `Space management` and `Water detection` stay English | `Konservierung`, English module names in German copy (`Indoor climate`, `Preservation`) |
| **German (`de`)** | Sensor / product names | English catalogue tokens; approved overrides (`Wasserdetektor`, `Außen Sensor`, `Range Extender und Bracket`) | `Feuchtesensor`, `Öffnen/Schließen`, `Humidity Sensor`, `Range Extender and Bracket` |
| **German (`de`)** | Preservation product terms | `Erhaltungsindex`, `Erhaltungsheizung`, … | `Preservation Index`, `Preservationsheizung`, … |
| **German (`de`)** | Relative humidity | `r. F.` or `relative Luftfeuchtigkeit` / `Luftfeuchtigkeit` | `RH`, `RF`, `rF`, `relative Feuchte` |
| **German (`de`)** | Conjunction punctuation | `XX und YY` or split sentences | `, und` (comma immediately before *und*) |
| **German (`de`)** | Standard noun capitalization | `Sensoren`, `Entscheidungen` (generic prose nouns) | Lowercase nouns (`sensor`, `entscheidungen`) in prose |
| **Danish / Swedish (`da` / `sv`)** | Sentence case (mirror `en`) | `sensor`, `sensorer`; hyphenated compounds (`Humidity-sensoren`, `CO2-sensor`) | English Title Case (`CO2 Sensor`, `Temperature Sensor`) |
| **Danish / Swedish (`da` / `sv`)** | Product suffixes in prose | `Humidity-sensoren`, `CO2-sensorn` | `Humidity sensoren` (space before Scandinavian suffix) |

Automated checks: `npm run check:locale` (also runs via pre-commit when
`src/data/**/*.ts` is staged). Canonical term lists: `src/data/deTermLocks.ts`.

