`forbiddenEnglishModuleTokens`, `forbiddenSensorTokens`,
`forbiddenEnglishSensorTokens`, and `forbiddenPreservationTermsDe` in
`de-term-locks.json`.

### Em dashes (`en`, `da`, `de`, `sv`)

Use em dashes (—) sparingly in **all locales**. At most **one em dash per
sentence**; at most **two per paragraph**, and only when sentences are short
and distinct. Stacking 2–3 dashes in one sentence or paragraph reads heavy on
the page.

| Rule | Do | Don't |
|------|----|-------|
| **Density** | One dash per sentence where it clearly adds emphasis or contrast | Paired asides (`— X —`), list-in-dash patterns, or 2–3 dashes in one sentence |
| **Paired asides** | Commas, parentheses, or a sentence split | `when you order — Air, Space, or Water — you get…` |
| **Lists in dashes** | Commas or parentheses: `(baseline, measure, analyse, remediate, verify)` | `baseline — measure, analyse — verify` |
| **Product labels** | Colon: `RoomAlyzer Air: indoor climate` | `RoomAlyzer Air — indoor climate` |
| **Product names** | Keep RoomAlyzer line and product names unchanged | Translate or re-case product names |
| **Translations** | Mirror the reduced dash count; use locale-appropriate punctuation | Literal dash-for-dash copy from English |

**Keep a single dash when it works:** a strong aside, contrast, or label where
commas or parentheses read worse. One dash in an SEO `<title>` separator is
fine if it is the only dash in that field (e.g. `Articles — every guide | …`).

**Prefer instead of a second dash:** commas, parentheses, colons, or splitting
into two sentences.

**Examples (English):**

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `when you order — Air, Space, or Water — you get everything` | `when you order RoomAlyzer Air, Space, or Water, you get everything` |
| `measures — PI/TWPI, mould risk, EN 15757 — for museums` | `measures (PI/TWPI, mould risk, EN 15757) for museums` |
| `before a battery runs flat — not after — so you can plan` | `before a battery runs flat, not after, so you can plan` |
| `The teams that champion — and approve — space decisions` | `The teams that champion and approve space decisions` |

**Out of scope:** UI/data glyphs (e.g. `"—"` as a compare-table “no value”
marker), code comments, and JSDoc unless they render on the public site.

### Localization content rules (names, places, standards)

When translating or localizing copy (`da` / `de` / `sv`), follow these rules
in addition to the product-name rules above:

| Category | Rule |
|----------|------|
| **Person names** | Never translate (team, quotes, bylines). |
| **Customer org / brand names** | Use the **official registered name** (e.g. `Erzdiözese Freiburg`, `Evangelische Kirche in Hessen und Nassau`, `Dansk Industri`, `Sweco`). Do not paraphrase into another language. |
| **Danish municipalities (customers)** | Use **locale-appropriate government label + place name**: `Varde Kommune` (da), `Gemeinde Varde` (de), `Varde kommun` (sv). Keep geographic spelling (`Solrød`, `Holbæk`). No erroneous possessives (e.g. not `Gribskovs kommun`). |
| **Geographic proper nouns** | Keep official spelling (`Freiburg`, `Roskilde`, `Hessen`). |
| **Standards and acronyms** | Keep the **official identifier** unchanged: `EN 15757`, `GDPR`, `CO₂`, `ISO 27001`, `MQTT`, `BR18`, `DGNB`, etc. Translate only the explanatory prose around them. |
| **Locale-specific regulations** | May name local rules (`BR18`, `APV`, `EHF`/`PEPPOL`) but on non-DK locales add jurisdiction context or “or your local equivalent” where relevant. |
| **Glossary terms** | Keep `term` and `anchor` as canonical identifiers; translate `short` and `detail` only. |
| **Sensor `heroTitle`** | Do not add “Sensor”/“sensor” suffixes in i18n overlays; use English catalogue titles + `localizedSensorName()` for approved DE exceptions only. |

