### Sensor dimension photography (required for new sensors)

Whenever a **new sensor** is added to the catalogue **and** it has a physical-dimensions
gallery on its product page, you **must** complete the bracket-calibration workflow.
Do not ship hand-tuned overlay coordinates in presets.

**Checklist (all steps required):**

1. Add the side-view dimension source PNG to `Pictures/Sensors/Dimensions/`.
2. Add a `{ source, targets }` row in [`scripts/lib/dimension-image-mappings.mjs`](scripts/lib/dimension-image-mappings.mjs).
3. Run `npm run sync-sensor-dimensions` (syncs WebP into `public/images/sensors/` **and**
   regenerates [`src/data/dimensionBracketCalibration.ts`](src/data/dimensionBracketCalibration.ts)).
4. Add the sensor entry in [`src/data/sensorDimensions.ts`](src/data/sensorDimensions.ts) with
   the correct overlay preset:
   - `bracketSide` — standard side-view bracket layout (most sensors)
   - `bracketSideOpenClose` — open/close small and large units
   - `bracketSideWaterCompact` / `bracketSideWaterPro` — water detector / water rope variants
     (IP label stays manual in the preset; `h`/`w` come from calibration)
   - `bracketIsometric` — temperature / desk coin layout only (explicit coords; not slot-calibrated)
5. Commit the regenerated `dimensionBracketCalibration.ts` with the sensor change.

**When dimension art changes** for an existing sensor, re-run `npm run sync-sensor-dimensions`
and commit the updated calibration file — do not manually nudge `x`/`y`/`dy` in presets.

Label positions are resolved at render time by [`src/lib/sensors/resolve-dimension-labels.ts`](src/lib/sensors/resolve-dimension-labels.ts)
from calibration data keyed by WebP basename. Presets declare **which** labels to show (`slot: "h" | "w"`), not pixel positions.


