## Module landing pages (locked base structure)

Every module landing page must ship the same **eight base sections** in this
overall flow. **Content and per-module styling are flexible**; removing or
reordering base sections is not.

Canonical order:

1. Hero — breadcrumbs, title, accent, lead, Book demo + Get an offer CTAs
2. Top picture — dashboard, editorial gallery, or sensor spotlight (placement
   in hero or below is per-module)
3. Challenges — intro prose + `ModuleChallengeCards`
4. How RoomAlyzer solves it — `ModuleCapabilitiesIntro` + `ModuleFeatureTabs`
5. Who it is for — two audience cards
6. Related module — `ModuleCrossLink` redirect
7. FAQ — `ModuleFaqSection`
8. CTA — featured `CtaBand`

**Authoritative template:** [`ModuleLandingPage.astro`](src/components/modules/ModuleLandingPage.astro).
New rich modules should prefer it + props over bespoke markup. Bespoke pages
that already follow the base (e.g. [`indoor-climate.astro`](src/pages/[lang]/modules/indoor-climate.astro),
[`space-management.astro`](src/pages/[lang]/modules/space-management.astro)) may
keep one-off hero/top-picture treatment.

### Allowed without approval

- **Top picture:** dashboard in hero, dashboard below hero, `heroVisual="gallery"`,
  sensor spotlight in hero or as its own section (preservation, water-detection,
  space-management patterns)
- **Challenges ↔ solution swap** via `capabilitiesBeforeChallenges={true}` only
  (preservation, water-detection)
- **Per-module props:** `challengeIconSet`, horizontal challenge layout,
  `revealBodyOnSelect`, `audiencesOnStone`, `secondaryAudienceIcon`, image classes
- **Hero variants:** `inlineTitleAccent`, split visual, temporary event teasers
  (indoor-climate ARCHIVISTICA pattern)
- **Content:** all i18n, images, FAQ items, feature tabs, cross-link targets,
  hub registry (`src/data/hubs/modules.ts`, `src/data/i18n/*.ts`, `*Images.ts`)

### Thin module pages (interim)

Routes via [`modules/[slug].astro`](src/pages/[lang]/modules/[slug].astro) +
[`ModulePageContent.astro`](src/components/content/ModulePageContent.astro) ship
a reduced body today. The **target** for every module is the full eight-section
base. Do not remove or further simplify thin pages; do not invent alternate thin
layouts. Upgrades should grow toward the rich base (`ModuleLandingPage` or
equivalent sections). Copy edits inside existing thin sections need no approval.

### Out of scope

Modules hub index ([`modules/index.astro`](src/pages/[lang]/modules/index.astro))
— card grid, not a module landing.

### Confirmation required

If a request removes, skips, merges, or reorders base sections beyond the
challenges ↔ solution swap; adds a new persistent section between base sections;
or refactors `ModuleLandingPage.astro` to drop a section slot, ask first:
"Module landing page base structure is locked per project rules — are you sure
you want to change it?"

## Logo carousel (locked)

The customer logo carousel — the `LogoMarquee.astro` component, its
markup, CSS, JavaScript, the customer roster, the per-customer URLs, and
the logo asset files under `public/logos/` — is **frozen** and must not
be modified in any way (size, spacing, speed, colours, hover effect,
animation, drag behaviour, list contents, ordering, links, or assets).

If a future user request would touch any of the above, you MUST first
ask the user to confirm explicitly that they really want to change the
locked carousel before making the edit. Phrase it as a direct yes/no
confirmation, e.g.: "The logo carousel is locked per project rules — are
you sure you want to change it?"

The only exception is **moving the `<LogoMarquee />` invocation up or
down within a page** (i.e. its vertical position relative to other
sections, with no changes to the component itself). Even this exception
requires explicit confirmation from the user before being applied.
